# syscall_x86_64_linux.cyr — x86_64 wrapper backfill for stdlib gaps
#
# Self-gated with `#ifdef CYRIUS_ARCH_X86_64` so this file ships in the
# bundled `dist/phylax.cyr` alongside the aarch64 peer; only the matching
# arch's block compiles in any given consumer build.
#
# ⚠ CURRENTLY EMPTY BY DESIGN — do not delete the file.
#
# It used to define `sys_stat`, `sys_fstat` and `sys_rename`. As of the
# cyrius 6.5.x stdlib all three exist upstream and are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the
# copies here (`lib/syscalls_x86_64_linux.cyr:341` / `:414` and
# `lib/syscalls_linux_common.cyr:146`), so the local copies bought nothing
# and cost three `duplicate fn ... last definition wins` warnings per build.
# Removed at the 1.2.6 P(-1) closeout.
#
# The file itself stays because the aarch64 peer is NOT empty: aarch64 Linux
# deprecated the bare `rename(2)`, so `src/syscall_aarch64_linux.cyr` still
# has to compose one through `renameat`. Keeping both peers in `[lib]` keeps
# the two arches symmetrical in the manifest and leaves an obvious home for
# the next x86_64-only gap.

#ifdef CYRIUS_ARCH_X86_64

#endif
